# --- generated project data ------------------------------------------------
#
# Everything under projects/ is produced by running the pipeline: uploaded
# source documents, stage artifacts, renders, logs. It is local to whoever ran
# it and must not enter the repository.
#
# An earlier version of this file listed `projects/*/chapters/*/audio/` and
# similar — a layout the code never used. The patterns silently matched nothing,
# so a demo project (including an uploaded PDF) was staged for commit. Ignoring
# the whole directory and keeping one placeholder is both simpler and immune to
# the layout changing again.
projects/*
!projects/.gitkeep

# derived index — rebuildable from files (ADR 0005)
.index/

# --- python ----------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- node ------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/

# --- secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
.env

# --- vendored upstream source (vendor/README.md) ----------------------------
#
# Manim, Revideo and Motion Canvas, cloned shallowly so the code that drives
# them can be read. Nothing imports or runs from here -- the working copies come
# from pip and npm -- so it is 49MB of other people's code, under their own
# licences, that this repository has no reason to carry. Delete these two lines
# to commit it anyway; the pipeline behaves identically either way.
vendor/
!vendor/README.md

# --- stray clones ----------------------------------------------------------
# A nested git repository committed as a directory becomes a broken gitlink
# that nobody can check out. Ignored so it cannot be staged by accident.
acedemic-explainer-video-pipeline/
renderers/.self-test.json
renderers/revideo/output/
renderers/revideo/*.log
